# Unearth's "If it would leave the battlefield, exile it instead of putting it anywhere else" (CR 702.84a) is a replacement
# effect (CR 614.1a), ordered by the permanent's controller with the others that would change the move (CR 616.1). Bot1 loots
# Phyrexian Dragon Engine into its graveyard on turn 1; Bot2 has Dauthi Voidwalker by turn 2. On turn 3 Bot1 unearths the
# Engine (declining its rummage) and Bolts it: as it would be put into the graveyard, Bot1 takes the Voidwalker's exile first,
# and the Engine is exiled with a void counter (unearth's no longer applies, CR 616.1f). On turn 4 Bot2 sacrifices the
# Voidwalker, chooses the Engine among Bot1's void-countered cards (the sacrificed Black Lotus and the Bolt are the others) and casts it.

